  "summary": "The screened region (indices 605–729) shows a sustained, accelerating displacement across N, E, and U axes without any opposing return or platform within the allowed context [570, 729]. The motion is coherent and monotonic: N rises from ~5.9 to >37, E from ~4.2 to >24, U drops from ~-4.6 to <-26. Inflection points near indices 680 and 710 reflect changes in acceleration rate but do not constitute reversals or offsets. No temporary offset interval is confirmed: onset is gradual (no sharp step), interior is sustained acceleration, and no return is observed before index 729. Missing samples (e.g., at indices 632, 652, 662, 672, 682, 692, 702, 712, 722) do not provide evidence of recovery. Thus, the trend is interpreted as long-term deformation/drift, not a temporary offset."
